  "obelix_metadata_fields": {
    "conductivity_type": "OBELiX's primary column 'Ionic conductivity (S cm-1)' is an author-curated 'best available' value; a separate 'IC (Total)'/'IC (Bulk)' split exists but is populated for <5% of rows (29/599 and 28/599 respectively), so the primary column cannot be verified row-by-row as uniformly bulk or total conductivity.",
    "temperature_field": "None -- OBELiX has no explicit per-row temperature column; the dataset is curated by its own authors as room-temperature values, not independently re-verified per row here.",
    "measurement_protocol_field": "None.",
    "units": "S cm^-1 (matches Hargreaves; no unit harmonization needed).",
    "aggregation_across_measurements": "One reported value per OBELiX row; no explicit multi-measurement aggregation field."
  },
  "hargreaves_metadata_fields": {
    "conductivity_type": "No bulk/total/grain-boundary field at all.",
    "temperature_field": "'temperature' (degrees C), per-row, range 5-873 C in the raw file; this project's RT window is [15,35] C (fixed pre-analysis, reports/npj/n1_external_data_audit.md).",
    "measurement_protocol_field": "None beyond 'source' (literature DOI).",
    "units": "S cm^-1 (matches OBELiX).",
    "aggregation_across_measurements": "This project's own N2 pipeline aggregates repeated RT-window rows of the same reduced formula to their MEDIAN log10(conductivity) (hargreaves_cohort.AGGREGATION_RULE); the raw Hargreaves file itself has no aggregation field, most repeats are Arrhenius-series multi-temperature measurements of the same sample."
  },
  "compatibility_gap_finding": "Neither database's headline scalar target is a verified, uniform bulk-vs-total quantity: OBELiX's primary column mixes an unlabeled majority with a <5% Total/Bulk-flagged minority, and Hargreaves has no bulk/total field whatsoever. Both report S/cm and both are treated by this project as 'a single, author-reported conductivity value' rather than a verified bulk value -- this is a genuine label-definition compatibility gap that predates and is independent of any modeling choice.",
